{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>על זאת</b> — that You bear iniquity." "<b>לעת מצוא</b> — like 'Seek YHWH when He is found,' and 'You shall seek from there HaShem your Elohim and you shall find.' Or, when his heart is found cleared of thoughts and free from his affairs and needs, then he prays, in the manner of 'Therefore Your servant found his heart.'" "The meaning of <b>שטף מים רבים</b> — an allusion to drowning his enemies in water, like 'Let him sweep me away from many waters.' Or death and illnesses, and he likens them to waters that have grown powerful. And the meaning of <b>רק</b> is 'only,' that the waters distress others, and it is as though he is bound with Him [so] they will not reach him — and its like is many in our language."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:13.841522998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}